Relevant columns and their potential usage  

• DICOM_METADATA."SeriesInstanceUID": identify the target MR series and to link to segmentation records  
• DICOM_METADATA."SOPInstanceUID": individual image objects whose modality we want to count  
• DICOM_METADATA."Modality": modality code of every SOP instance (“MR”, “SEG”, etc.)  
• SEGMENTATIONS."segmented_SeriesInstanceUID": SeriesInstanceUID that a segmentation refers to (connects segmentations with the MR series)  
• SEGMENTATIONS."SOPInstanceUID": SOPInstanceUID of every segmentation object  
• SEGMENTATIONS."SeriesInstanceUID": SeriesInstanceUID of the SEG series itself (useful when looking them up in DICOM_METADATA)  

Conditions that will probably be useful  

1. DICOM_METADATA."SeriesInstanceUID" = '1.3.6.1.4.1.14519.5.2.1.3671.4754.105976129314091491952445656147'  
2. SEGMENTATIONS."segmented_SeriesInstanceUID" = same UID above  
3. DICOM_METADATA."SOPInstanceUID" IN (the list of SOPInstanceUID returned from SEGMENTATIONS)  
4. Final grouping on DICOM_METADATA."Modality" and counting rows  

Below are ten exploratory Snowflake SQL queries (LIMIT 20 rows for sampling) that progress from simple inspection to the final analytic step.  

```sql
-- 1. Description: Peek at the MR‑series metadata row itself
SELECT *
FROM IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_METADATA
WHERE "SeriesInstanceUID" = '1.3.6.1.4.1.14519.5.2.1.3671.4754.105976129314091491952445656147'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: Count how many SOPInstances belong to that MR series
SELECT COUNT(*) AS "num_sop_mr"
FROM IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_METADATA
WHERE "SeriesInstanceUID" = '1.3.6.1.4.1.14519.5.2.1.3671.4754.105976129314091491952445656147';
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: List all segmentation rows that reference the MR series
SELECT *
FROM IDC.IDC_V17.SEGMENTATIONS
WHERE "segmented_SeriesInstanceUID" = '1.3.6.1.4.1.14519.5.2.1.3671.4754.105976129314091491952445656147'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: Distinct SOPInstanceUIDs of those segmentations
SELECT DISTINCT "SOPInstanceUID"
FROM IDC.IDC_V17.SEGMENTATIONS
WHERE "segmented_SeriesInstanceUID" = '1.3.6.1.4.1.14519.5.2.1.3671.4754.105976129314091491952445656147'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: Pull DICOM metadata for all segmentation SOPs (to get Modality codes)
SELECT dm.*
FROM IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_METADATA dm
JOIN (
      SELECT DISTINCT "SOPInstanceUID"
      FROM IDC.IDC_V17.SEGMENTATIONS
      WHERE "segmented_SeriesInstanceUID" = '1.3.6.1.4.1.14519.5.2.1.3671.4754.105976129314091491952445656147'
     ) seg
ON dm."SOPInstanceUID" = seg."SOPInstanceUID"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description: Count SOPInstances for those segmentation objects, by Modality
SELECT dm."Modality", COUNT(*) AS "num_sop_seg"
FROM IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_METADATA dm
JOIN (
      SELECT DISTINCT "SOPInstanceUID"
      FROM IDC.IDC_V17.SEGMENTATIONS
      WHERE "segmented_SeriesInstanceUID" = '1.3.6.1.4.1.14519.5.2.1.3671.4754.105976129314091491952445656147'
     ) seg
ON dm."SOPInstanceUID" = seg."SOPInstanceUID"
GROUP BY dm."Modality"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description: Union all MR‑series SOPs with segmentation SOPs and view sample
SELECT "SOPInstanceUID", "SeriesInstanceUID", "Modality"
FROM IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_METADATA
WHERE "SeriesInstanceUID" = '1.3.6.1.4.1.14519.5.2.1.3671.4754.105976129314091491952445656147'

UNION ALL

SELECT dm."SOPInstanceUID", dm."SeriesInstanceUID", dm."Modality"
FROM IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_METADATA dm
JOIN (
      SELECT DISTINCT "SOPInstanceUID"
      FROM IDC.IDC_V17.SEGMENTATIONS
      WHERE "segmented_SeriesInstanceUID" = '1.3.6.1.4.1.14519.5.2.1.3671.4754.105976129314091491952445656147'
     ) seg
ON dm."SOPInstanceUID" = seg."SOPInstanceUID"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description: Aggregate counts by Modality over the union set
SELECT "Modality", COUNT(*) AS "num_sop_total"
FROM (
      SELECT "SOPInstanceUID", "Modality"
      FROM IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_METADATA
      WHERE "SeriesInstanceUID" = '1.3.6.1.4.1.14519.5.2.1.3671.4754.105976129314091491952445656147'
      
      UNION ALL
      
      SELECT dm."SOPInstanceUID", dm."Modality"
      FROM IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_METADATA dm
      JOIN (
            SELECT DISTINCT "SOPInstanceUID"
            FROM IDC.IDC_V17.SEGMENTATIONS
            WHERE "segmented_SeriesInstanceUID" = '1.3.6.1.4.1.14519.5.2.1.3671.4754.105976129314091491952445656147'
           ) seg
      ON dm."SOPInstanceUID" = seg."SOPInstanceUID"
     ) u
GROUP BY "Modality"
ORDER BY "num_sop_total" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description: Identify the modality with the greatest number of SOP instances (top‑1)
SELECT "Modality", COUNT(*) AS "num_sop_total"
FROM (
      SELECT "SOPInstanceUID", "Modality"
      FROM IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_METADATA
      WHERE "SeriesInstanceUID" = '1.3.6.1.4.1.14519.5.2.1.3671.4754.105976129314091491952445656147'
      
      UNION ALL
      
      SELECT dm."SOPInstanceUID", dm."Modality"
      FROM IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_METADATA dm
      JOIN (
            SELECT DISTINCT "SOPInstanceUID"
            FROM IDC.IDC_V17.SEGMENTATIONS
            WHERE "segmented_SeriesInstanceUID" = '1.3.6.1.4.1.14519.5.2.1.3671.4754.105976129314091491952445656147'
           ) seg
      ON dm."SOPInstanceUID" = seg."SOPInstanceUID"
     ) u
GROUP BY "Modality"
ORDER BY "num_sop_total" DESC
LIMIT 1;
```

```sql
-- 10. Description: Full detail of SOP instances for the winning modality (replace <WINNING_MODALITY> after seeing results)
SELECT *
FROM (
      SELECT "SOPInstanceUID", "Modality"
      FROM IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_METADATA
      WHERE "SeriesInstanceUID" = '1.3.6.1.4.1.14519.5.2.1.3671.4754.105976129314091491952445656147'
      
